  "objective": "# External idea (operator-selected)\n\n**Mode:** pure Cursor Ultra-lite (model/auto per Cursor mode; no Codex / hybrid)\n**App name intent:** BendCoach AI\n**Positioning:** paid AI conduit-bending coach for electricians — field bend math + photo markup coaching (NOT a brand clone of QuickBend)\n**Reference:** QuickBend / Bret-H.-Hardman.QuickBend — category reference only; do NOT copy brand, UI, assets, or unauthorized scraping. Numeric outputs must be labeled as assistive, not a substitute for code/engineer judgment. Include unit-system explanation (imperial/metric as product supports).\n\n## Idea\nBuild a paid AI conduit-bending coach for electricians: chat for bend math in plain English, import job-site photos to recognize bends/markups, generate diagram overlays, TTS step-by-step field coaching—one-time unlock for pro bend packs.\n\n## Pricing intent\nOne-time unlock for pro bend packs (paid unlock path). Core free path may allow a limited demo coach session if needed for App Store clarity; paid unlocks pro bend packs + full coach features.\n\n## Four permissions (hard rule — first build into Info.plist + testable features)\nDefault all four with usage strings fitting BendCoach; each fully usable and measurable (sim UI/journey OK; device-only → 真机待测, does not block delivery):\n- **Camera:** capture job-site bend / markup photos\n- **Photo library:** import field photos to recognize bend types\n- **Microphone:** spoken questions for bend math / field dictation\n- **Speech recognition:** speech-to-text feeding chat bend-math\nExtensions supplement; do **not** replace the core sell path: bend-math chat → photo import/recognize → diagram overlay → TTS step coaching.\n\n## Constraints\n- Privacy local-first; minimize cloud retention of job-site photos\n- Do not copy QuickBend brand/UI; label numbers as assistive; unit-system UX clear\n- Core sell-path must be runtime-tested; simulator-impossible items mark as 真机待测 (does not block delivery)\n- Only core defects block delivery; non-core → known_issues; max 2 repair rounds\n- Prefer product delivery push to git@github.com:xy-gty/xy-gty.git\n- Feishu registration / delivery card deferred (operator instruction)\n- No hand-editing MAP / receipts\n- App name, UI, store copy must avoid owner-forbidden languages when specified\n- Stagger simulator lease vs factory-prod-1 (CuePartner / active run); prefer UDID other than whatever prod-1 holds\n\n## Slot / worktree\nfactory-prod-2 · slot B · continuous packaging after DocBrief delivered\n",
